**Web Scraping Function in JavaScript**
=====================================

Below is a basic example of a JavaScript function that uses the `axios` library to scrape a website. This function will fetch the HTML content of a webpage and return it as a string.

```javascript
// Import the axios library
const axios = require('axios');

/**
 * Scrapes a website and returns the HTML content as a string.
 * @param {string} url - The URL of the webpage to scrape.
 * @returns {Promise<string>} A promise that resolves with the HTML content of the webpage.
 */
async function scrapeWebsite(url) {
  try {
    // Send a GET request to the webpage
    const response = await axios.get(url);

    // Return the HTML content of the webpage
    return response.data;
  } catch (error) {
    // If an error occurs, return the error message
    return error.message;
  }
}

// Example usage:
scrapeWebsite('https://www.example.com')
  .then(html => console.log(html))
  .catch(error => console.error(error));
```

